iga-surface-reactions.out
Prescribed 2D surface motions: analytical reactions for native and degree-one IGA elements
StaticStructural nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 rtolv 1.e-11 maxiter 10 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 2dPlaneStress
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 12 nelem 6 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 5 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 5
# Horizontal axisymmetric segment, shifted rigidly in Z by 0.1.
node 1 coords 2 1.0 0.0
node 2 coords 2 2.0 0.0
node 3 coords 2 1.0 0.0
node 4 coords 2 2.0 0.0
# Reversed cylindrical generatrix, R=2, shifted radially by 0.1.
node 5 coords 2 2.0 1.0
node 6 coords 2 2.0 0.0
node 7 coords 2 2.0 1.0
node 8 coords 2 2.0 0.0
# Planar unit segment, with the second endpoint moved by (0,1).
node 9 coords 2 0.0 0.0
node 10 coords 2 1.0 0.0
node 11 coords 2 0.0 0.0
node 12 coords 2 1.0 0.0
axilinesurface 1 nodes 2 1 2 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
bsplineaxisymsurfaceelement 2 nodes 2 3 4 crosssect 1 knotvectoru 2 0 1 degree 1 1 nip 2 nlgeo 1
axilinesurface 3 nodes 2 5 6 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
bsplineaxisymsurfaceelement 4 nodes 2 7 8 crosssect 1 knotvectoru 2 0 1 degree 1 1 nip 2 nlgeo 1
lineplanestrainsurface 5 nodes 2 9 10 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
bsplineplanestrainsurfaceelement 6 nodes 2 11 12 crosssect 1 knotvectoru 2 0 1 degree 1 1 nip 2 nlgeo 1
simplesurfacecs 1 material 1
surfacetensionmat 1 gamma1 0.5 d 1.0
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0.0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0.1 set 2
BoundaryCondition 3 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0.1 set 3
BoundaryCondition 4 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0.0 set 4
BoundaryCondition 5 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 1.0 set 5
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.0
Set 1 nodes 8 1 2 3 4 9 10 11 12
Set 2 nodes 4 5 6 7 8
Set 3 nodes 4 1 2 3 4
Set 4 nodes 6 5 6 7 8 9 11
Set 5 nodes 2 10 12
#
# Reference reactions are derivatives of the surface energy, not recorded solver output.
# Axisymmetry, per radian: E = gamma * L_current * (r1+r2)/2.
# Plane strain, unit out-of-plane thickness: E = gamma * L_current.
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-9
## Horizontal axisymmetric segment: R is unchanged by the rigid axial shift.
#REACTION tStep 1 number 1 dof 1 value -0.5
#REACTION tStep 1 number 1 dof 2 value 0.0
#REACTION tStep 1 number 2 dof 1 value 1.0
#REACTION tStep 1 number 2 dof 2 value 0.0
#REACTION tStep 1 number 3 dof 1 value -0.5
#REACTION tStep 1 number 3 dof 2 value 0.0
#REACTION tStep 1 number 4 dof 1 value 1.0
#REACTION tStep 1 number 4 dof 2 value 0.0
## Reversed vertical segment: hoop stretch 2.1/2 = 1.05 for both formulations.
#REACTION tStep 1 number 5 dof 1 value 0.25
#REACTION tStep 1 number 5 dof 2 value 1.05
#REACTION tStep 1 number 6 dof 1 value 0.25
#REACTION tStep 1 number 6 dof 2 value -1.05
#REACTION tStep 1 number 7 dof 1 value 0.25
#REACTION tStep 1 number 7 dof 2 value 1.05
#REACTION tStep 1 number 8 dof 1 value 0.25
#REACTION tStep 1 number 8 dof 2 value -1.05
## Planar segment: gamma * current unit tangent = (1,1)/(2*sqrt(2)).
#REACTION tStep 1 number 9 dof 1 value -0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 9 dof 2 value -0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 10 dof 1 value 0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 10 dof 2 value 0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 11 dof 1 value -0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 11 dof 2 value -0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 12 dof 1 value 0.3535533905932738
#REACTION tStep 1 number 12 dof 2 value 0.3535533905932738
## IST_DeformationGradientTensor = 91. Native elements store the hoop component as
## material F22; IGA elements use the global (R,Z,theta) frame, where it is F33.
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 2 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 2 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 3 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 2 irule 0 gp 2 keyword 91 component 3 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 3 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.05
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 3 irule 0 gp 2 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.05
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 4 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 3 value 1.05
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 4 irule 0 gp 2 keyword 91 component 3 value 1.05
## The same planar normal displacement gradient is material F31 for the native
## element and global F21 for IGA; both must survive the stored-stress reaction path.
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 5 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 8 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 6 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 9 value 1.0
#%END_CHECK%
